+{"time":"2026-08-28T11:55:09Z","branch":"empty-lattice-path","note":"No prior master guidance, global-memory findings, verifier traces, or accepted facts were returned. Represent unoccupied squares as a monotone path from (1,n) to (m,1), with E increasing i and S decreasing j. Initially the word is E^(m-1)S^(n-1). A legal move replaces an empty ES corner by SE. Conversely, in the complement configuration of any path, a local SE corner can be reversed: the northeast fourth square is off the path and hence occupied, and sliding its coin northwest changes SE to ES. Repeatedly decreasing the number of S-before-E inversions reaches the initial word. Thus reachable configurations biject with words containing m-1 E's and n-1 S's, counted by binomial(m+n-2,m-1). Edge cases m=1 or n=1 also give 1."}

